Stanislav Traykov wrote:
> Dex wrote on 10/13/2003 06:59 PM:
>> What are the chances for wresting a final charge out of a cursed wand of
>> wishing, and the chances of it actually getting what I wish for?

I'm assuming that you don't have bad luck, as that affects both parts.

> The chances would be 1/121 * 99 = 9/11.

Eh? Some dodgy reasoning must've occurred to reach that calculation...

When you zap a wand, the charges are checked and the attempt aborted if
it has negative charges (cancelled) or none and you don't hit the 1/121
chance of it working anyway.

Then, if the wand is cursed, there is a one in one hundred chance of it
exploding and you, obviously, not getting your wish.

As far as getting what you ask for is concerned, it depends on what you
ask for and your luck at the time but not, IIRC, the state of the wand.

So you can expect 121-ish turns to activate the wand and you have a 99%
chance of getting a wish when it eventually works and a 1% chance of it
exploding.  The overall chance of you getting a wish depends on whether
you might die in any given period while (possibly) holding the `z' key;
if you're sensible, the chance is very nearly 99%.

